## Exact match

```
{
  "find": {
    "Vendor name": "{sender_name}"
  }
}
```

JSON

The query checks the "Vendor name" in the dataset and compares it to the value of the "Vendor name" field extracted from the document. To refer to the "Vendor name" field, we used its schema ID - `sender_name`.

Even though exact match can be achieved using `find` method instead of `aggregate` ([see below](https://knowledge-base.rossum.ai/help/docs/configuration-examples-5#exact-match-caseinsensitive)), it is still recommended to use `aggregate` because it's often necessary to specify `$project` stage:

```
{
  "aggregate": [
    {
      "$match": {
        "Vendor name": "{sender_name}"
      }
    },
    {
      "$project": {
        "Supplier Name": 1
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

